      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no consensus among sociologists that secularization alone guarantees greater stability; instead, the \"decline of religion\" is a highly contested topic with opposing theories. While some argue that secular rational-legal authorities like democratic governments provide more flexible governance in modern societies, others fear that the erosion of traditional community ties leads to increased atomization and social fragmentation. Consequently, most contemporary research suggests that the impact on social order is complex and depends on how well new secular institutions can fill the void left by religious influence.",
